<TeXmacs|1.0.7.9>

<style|tmdoc>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Mathematical formulas>

  One of the main purposes of <TeXmacs> is to edit mathematical formulas. If
  the cursor is inside a<nbsp>formula (<abbr|i.e.> inside ``math mode''),
  then the mode sensitive menus and toolbars provide buttons for entering
  common mathematical constructs. Similarly, as will be detailed in this
  section, the bahaviour of the keyboard changes so as to allow for the rapid
  typing of mathematical symbols. For instance, typing <key|- \<gtr\>>
  inserts the arrow <math|\<rightarrow\>>.

  Mathematical input provides structured fractions, scripts, delimiters and
  symbols. The editor also offers optional, explicit formula correction
  commands; ordinary typing does not enforce grammatical validity.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|Incorporating mathematical formulas into
    documents|keyboard/man-enter-math.en.tm>

    <branch|Mathematical symbols|keyboard/man-symbols.en.tm>

